  On the published target, copying today's fire unchanged already scores
  0.9474. The best network in section 15 scores 0.9922, so everything a model
  contributes -- every channel, every parameter -- is worth 0.045 of AP on top of
  a rule that ignores the data.

  On the spread-only target the same rule scores 0.0036, which is chance
  (0.0036) by construction, and the best network scores 0.3046. That is the
  whole reason section 15 measures channels there: the published framing
  leaves them fighting over the last few percent of a saturated metric.
